{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.distinguishes_bare_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.distinguishes_bare_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/MirrorSwapCompatibility.lean#L103-L116","doc":"**And it DOES separate `x` from its bare mirror, whenever it is nonzero.**\nThe corpus's claim, in the same breath as its compatibility: the two facts sit\ntogether without tension, on different arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.cannot_distinguish_mirror_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.cannot_distinguish_mirror_swap","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/MirrorSwapCompatibility.lean#L93-L101","doc":"**The invariant is blind to the double image.**  `mu` takes the same value\non `x` and on `mirror (swap x)`, so it cannot be used to separate them — which\nis precisely the configuration in which a link is amphichiral while an ordered\ninvariant still distinguishes it from its bare mirror. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.negBoth_comp_fixes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.negBoth_comp_fixes","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/MirrorSwapCompatibility.lean#L86-L91","doc":"**Two negations compose to a fixed point.**  If both `mirror` and `swap`\nnegate `mu`, their composite preserves it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.Negates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.MirrorSwapCompatibility.Negates","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/MirrorSwapCompatibility.lean#L83-L84","doc":"An operation negates the invariant `mu`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}